        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="what action the listener imagines taking" data-hint="Listen for the linked What would you do and the closed-venue condition." data-fix="The question asks what action the listener imagines taking if the venue closed."><p class="quiz-question">2. What information does the linked question request?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="what action the listener imagines taking">what action the listener imagines taking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="when the venue definitely closed yesterday">when the venue definitely closed yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="who has already purchased the venue">who has already purchased the venue</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Start with a smaller pilot." data-hint="Listen for If I were you and the contracted advice result I’d start." data-fix="The advice is to start with a smaller pilot."><p class="quiz-question">3. What advice does the third line give?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Start with a smaller pilot.">Start with a smaller pilot.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Cancel every future project.">Cancel every future project.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Spend the entire budget immediately.">Spend the entire budget immediately.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Recording classes would become an available option." data-hint="Listen for could offer, which presents an available option rather than a guaranteed decision." data-fix="With more room, recording classes would become an available option."><p class="quiz-question">4. What does <span class="ex">could offer</span> communicate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Recording classes would become an available option.">Recording classes would become an available option.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Recording classes would become compulsory.">Recording classes would become compulsory.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The center offered the classes yesterday.">The center offered the classes yesterday.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had." data-hint="Listen to the form after each contraction: base add versus participle added." data-fix="In We’d add, ’d means would; in we’d added, ’d means had."><p class="quiz-question">5. What does <span class="ex">’d</span> mean in the two final phrases?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had.">The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both contractions can only mean did.">Both contractions can only mean did.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both phrases are commands about tomorrow.">Both phrases are commands about tomorrow.</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor transcript and evidence notes</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">If a larger grant ARRIVED, we’d BUILD a studio.</span> Evidence: past-form distance for a remote future scenario.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">What would you DO if the venue CLOSED?</span> Evidence: linked /wədʒə/ and a requested imagined action.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">If I were YOU, I’d START with a smaller PILOT.</span> Evidence: conventional advice frame and contracted result.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">If we had more ROOM, we could OFFER recording classes.</span> Evidence: could presents an available option.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">With more room, we’d ADD a studio. By noon, we’d ADDED all the chairs.</span> Evidence: base <span class="ex">add</span> resolves <span class="ex">’d</span> as <span class="ex">would</span>; participle <span class="ex">added</span> resolves it as <span class="ex">had</span>.</li>
