  </section>

  <h2>Read one complete planning update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Riverside studio decision, Thursday afternoon</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">The team will learn on Friday whether its current grant application succeeded. If the grant arrives, it will rent Hall A for a six-week pilot. The current budget is $18,000, which is not enough for a recording booth. If the team had twice that budget, it would build one, and it could offer audio classes. Lena thinks a smaller pilot is safer. She tells Maya, “If I were you, I’d test the schedule before buying equipment.” The building manager says Sunday access is not available now. If the center could open on Sundays next year, it might add one weekend class.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the open Friday plan, imagined larger budget, available audio-class option, and advice to test the schedule from the update.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only the planning update</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It will rent Hall A for a six-week pilot." data-hint="The second sentence gives the planned response if the current grant succeeds." data-fix="If the grant arrives, the team will rent Hall A for a six-week pilot."><p class="quiz-question">1. What is the team’s open plan if the grant arrives?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It will rent Hall A for a six-week pilot.">It will rent Hall A for a six-week pilot.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It will immediately buy the entire building.">It will immediately buy the entire building.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It will cancel the grant application.">It will cancel the grant application.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="$36,000" data-hint="Twice the stated current budget of $18,000 is $36,000." data-fix="The imagined budget is $36,000, twice the current $18,000."><p class="quiz-question">2. How large is the imagined budget that would support a recording booth?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="$36,000">$36,000</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="$18,000">$18,000</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="$9,000">$9,000</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Audio classes would become an available option." data-hint="The update uses could offer after the imagined larger budget." data-fix="With twice the budget, audio classes would become an available option."><p class="quiz-question">3. What would the larger budget make possible, without guaranteeing that choice?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Audio classes would become an available option.">Audio classes would become an available option.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every resident would be required to attend.">Every resident would be required to attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Sunday access would already exist.">Sunday access would already exist.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Test the schedule before buying equipment." data-hint="Read the direct quotation introduced as Lena’s advice to Maya." data-fix="Lena advises Maya to test the schedule before buying equipment."><p class="quiz-question">4. What does Lena advise Maya to do first?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Test the schedule before buying equipment.">Test the schedule before buying equipment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Open on Sunday without permission.">Open on Sunday without permission.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Reject the current grant before Friday.">Reject the current grant before Friday.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build a hypothetical question and careful advice</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="what would the team do if the grant did not arrive" data-hint="Begin with What would the team do, then use statement order and did not plus arrive in the if-clause." data-fix="What would the team do if the grant did not arrive?" data-success-message="Correct. The result clause uses question order, while the if-clause keeps the grant before did not arrive.">
    <h3>Build 1: ask about an imagined failed application</h3><p class="tile-target">The application is still open. Temporarily imagine that the grant does not arrive and ask for the team’s response.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="grant">grant</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="team">team</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="not">not</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="what">What</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="arrive">arrive</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="if">if</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="do">do</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="did">did</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="would">would</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="if I were the coordinator I would start with a pilot" data-hint="Begin with If I were the coordinator, then build the result with I would plus the base verb start." data-fix="If I were the coordinator, I would start with a pilot." data-success-message="Correct. Were creates the careful imagined position, and would start gives the advice result.">
    <h3>Build 2: give advice from an imagined position</h3><p class="tile-target">Use careful hypothetical style to say what you recommend as the fictional coordinator.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="pilot">pilot</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="coordinator">coordinator</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="if">If</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="would">would</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="with">with</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="start">start</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="were">were</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair clause or modal form</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="would have" data-hint="The team does not have more space now; a neutral Second Conditional puts the past form in the if-clause." data-fix="If we had more space, we’d add a recording booth." data-why="Had creates distance from the current space, while would belongs in the imagined result. Would have here would not express the ordinary condition." data-success-message="Correct. Had belongs in the neutral imagined condition, while would add belongs in its result.">
    <h3>Repair 1: keep ordinary <span class="ex">would</span> in the result</h3><p>Tap the verb phrase that incorrectly places <span class="ex">would</span> in the neutral condition.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">we</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="would have">would have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="space">more space,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="add">we’d add</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="booth">a recording booth.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="moved" data-hint="Would requires a base verb in the imagined result." data-fix="If the venue closed next month, the team would move to Hall A." data-why="The modal would already carries the conditional meaning, so the lexical verb stays in its base form move." data-success-message="Correct. Move is the base verb required after would in the imagined result.">
    <h3>Repair 2: use the base verb after <span class="ex">would</span></h3><p>Tap the result verb that incorrectly uses a past form after <span class="ex">would</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="venue">the venue</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="closed">closed next month,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="team">the team</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="would">would</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="moved">moved</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hall">to Hall A.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="you would" data-hint="Question order places would before the subject you in the result clause." data-fix="What would you do if the grant did not arrive?" data-why="The result clause is the question: What would you do? The if-clause keeps ordinary statement order: if the grant did not arrive." data-success-message="Correct. Would moves before you in the question, while the if-clause keeps statement order.">
    <h3>Repair 3: put question order in the right clause</h3><p>Tap the two-word sequence that reverses the subject and modal incorrectly.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="what">What</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you would">you would</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">do</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">if</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="grant">the grant</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="did">did not arrive?</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it without exposing personal choices</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real income, budget, employer, career plans, housing, immigration status, family, health, schedule, location, political views, relationships, education record, or personal regrets. Use the fictional Riverside center. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Different present:</b> The center has one room. Imagine it had three rooms. State one expected consequence, one available option, and one uncertain possibility.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Remote future:</b> The director sees a citywide expansion as doubtful. Explain what the center would need and what it might offer if expansion happened.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Advice:</b> Maya is considering buying equipment before testing the schedule. Use <span class="ex">If I were you</span> and give a reason.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Tactful proposal:</b> The pilot feels too large. Ask <span class="ex">Would it help if...?</span>, then invite one alternative.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: lead a 75–90 second fictional planning discussion</h3>
    <p>Begin with one open First Conditional plan. Then explore one different present and one remote future with Second Conditional forms. Include one <span class="ex">would</span> consequence, one <span class="ex">could</span> option, one <span class="ex">might</span> possibility, one tactful piece of advice, and one follow-up question. Explain why each condition is open or deliberately distant.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener recover the speaker’s stance, the condition and result, the exact modal meaning, and whether <span class="ex">were</span> or <span class="ex">was</span> fits the chosen register?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved open versus distant framing, selected a result modal for its exact meaning, and treated were and informal was accurately.">
    <h3>Final check: defend the speaker’s choices</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the current grant arrives Friday, we’ll rent Hall A." data-hint="The result is due Friday, and the team has an active response plan, so preserve the open frame." data-fix="If the current grant arrives Friday, we’ll rent Hall A."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence presents the current grant as an open future path?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the current grant arrives Friday, we’ll rent Hall A.">If the current grant arrives Friday, we’ll rent Hall A.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the grant would arrive, we rented Hall A tomorrow.">If the grant would arrive, we rented Hall A tomorrow.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the grant had arrives, we’d renting Hall A.">If the grant had arrives, we’d renting Hall A.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If we had more room, we could offer recording classes." data-hint="The context asks for an available option, so use could plus the base verb offer." data-fix="If we had more room, we could offer recording classes."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence presents recording classes as an available option in the imagined larger space?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If we had more room, we could offer recording classes.">If we had more room, we could offer recording classes.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If we would have room, recording classes were compulsory.">If we would have room, recording classes were compulsory.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If we have room yesterday, we could offered classes.">If we have room yesterday, we could offered classes.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If I were you is the safest careful advice form; If I was you also occurs in informal speech." data-hint="Separate the careful target from a widespread informal U.S. pattern instead of calling the informal form impossible." data-fix="If I were you is the safest careful advice form; If I was you also occurs in informal speech."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which statement accurately describes the advice frame?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If I were you is the safest careful advice form; If I was you also occurs in informal speech.">If I were you is the safest careful advice form; If I was you also occurs in informal speech.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If I was you has no meaning in any variety of English.">If I was you has no meaning in any variety of English.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If I were you describes a finished event yesterday.">If I were you describes a finished event yesterday.</button></div></div>
    </div>
